# answered by claude-opus-5-5, prompt /lib/phil/senses b350a3107fa4, 2026-10-19
pursuit	one
good	one
aims	one
# The step from P1 to C moves "for some y" ahead of "for every x": from "each pursuit aims at some good" to "there is one good all pursuits aim at".
# That is a change in quantifier scope, not a change in sense.
# "good" in "some good" and in "the Chief Good" is formalized the same way. Its chiefness comes only from the wider quantifier, not from a second sense of the word.
